Compiling e2fsprogs inside /sources

1. Navigate to the sources directory and download e2fsprogs:

`cd /sources`
`curl -O https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/people/tytso/e2fsprogs/v1.47.0/e2fsprogs-1.47.0.tar.gz`

2. Extract the archive and enter the build directory:

`tar -xf e2fsprogs-1.47.0.tar.gz`
`cd e2fsprogs-1.47.0`

3. Create a dedicated build directory:

`mkdir build`
`cd build`

4. Configure, compile, and install e2fsprogs:

`../configure --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc --enable-elf-shlibs --disable-libblkid --disable-libuuid --disable-uuidd --disable-fsck`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`

5. Clean up the source directory:

`cd /sources`
`rm -rf e2fsprogs-1.47.0*`
